WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.067 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Our first guest tonight

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:03.169
is a six-time
Academy Award-nominated actress

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:05.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
and three-time
Tony and Emmy winner

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:06.139 size:88% position:44% line:92%
you know from such films

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:08.942 size:78% position:39%
as "Fatal Attraction"
and "101 Dalmatians."

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.010 size:88% position:44% line:92%
She stars in "The Wife,"

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:12.946
which opens in New York and L.A.
on Friday.

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:13.613 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.749
-May I also say, congratulations
to you, as well, Joan?

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:18.018
I don't think people give
the spouse enough credit.

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:22.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I give my...wife credit.
I...give her plenty of credit.

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.224 line:92%
-Oh, that's not what I meant.

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:25.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
I meant, you know,
the rest of the world --

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.360
the -- the critics, the readers,
and most of all --

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I know -- I know I'm
supposed to be impressed that,

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.799
somehow, you've wheedled
your way onto this flight,

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:33.733 size:81% position:41% line:92%
but I'm telling you --

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:37.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
I am not giving you permission
to write my biography.

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:38.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, would you please...
-Absolutely.

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:40.273
-...leave us alone?
-You made that abundantly clear.

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:41.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Fine. Good.
-I'm so sorry.

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:42.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just wanted to say
congratulations.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:43.276 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:44.778 size:88% position:44%
-Thank you for coming by
and saying hello today.

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:46.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean it sincerely.
Thank you.

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:48.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome back
to the show

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:50.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
our friend Glenn Close,
everybody.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.685 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:56.656 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:59.292 line:92%
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:01.528 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:03.830 line:92%
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:08.134 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hello.
-Hello.

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:12.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm so happy to see you.
-And good to see you.

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:14.808
-We -- This is, I feel --
This is very nice for me,

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:16.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we used to
see each other a lot more

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:17.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we lived
in the same building.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:19.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
And Rasheed says hello.

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:22.549
-Rasheed is the -- a doorman
who is very dear to my heart.

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:24.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And we miss him desperately.

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:25.985 line:92%
-And his baby was born, I think,

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:29.689 size:84% position:42%
he said like four hours
before or after Ashe.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:30.490 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes. So, we --

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.358
we have children that are
very close in the same age.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I stop by every now
and then to say hi to him,

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:36.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he's very upset
if I don't bring my children.

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:39.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm upset that -- that Ashe
wasn't born in our lobby.

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.167 line:92%
-Oh, Axel was the lobby baby.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, A-- Oh, Axel.
-Yeah.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:44.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm upset that Axel
wasn't born in our lobby.

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:46.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I know.
A lot of people, you know,

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:47.841
because we lived in that
building for a long time.

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:48.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And then my wife had

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:51.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
our baby Axel
in the new building

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:52.779 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and you guys missed out.

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:53.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We did.
-Yeah.

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:54.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
-We really did.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
-'Cause there were --
you could see a lot of stuff.

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:58.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:58.051 --> 00:01:58.985 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:03.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
Uh, this is a wonderful film.
-Thank you.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was a scintillating --
-A scintillating --

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:08.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A scintillating,
action-packed clip.

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:10.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I mean,
it is a wonderful...

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I think that's good.

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:14.634
I'm glad you're letting people
know that, because, very rarely,

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:17.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
as the performer in a film,
do you pick the clip.

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:19.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're often finding out
right back there

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.174 line:92%
which clip it was, as well.

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:21.975 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Yeah. Well, if my --

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:24.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
the character that I play
is very internalized.

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:28.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I mean, that's one
of the fascinating things I --

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:31.251 line:92%
I discovered playing her.

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:31.985 size:78% position:39% line:92%
So, I mean, in a way,

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:34.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's kind of
indicative of what's --

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:35.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, it's not.
-Yeah.

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:39.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-It's a really good movie.

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:41.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is a really good movie.
And it's --

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, Jonathan Pryce, who's
a wonderful actor, as well --

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:44.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-He plays your husband,

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:47.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
who is winning
a Nobel Prize for Literature,

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's really
a film that has a --

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:52.338
a great building tension
as to what it's been like

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be the wife
of this famous author...

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:56.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-...for, oh, many years.

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:59.245
Did you -- What drew you
to playing this character?

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:03.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Eh. Well, in -- in some ways,
first of all,

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:04.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd never played a character
like that before.

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:07.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't like to kind of
go over the same territory...

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:08.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-...emotionally.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:11.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've -- You know,
you're the same way, right?

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:14.260
-Yeah. That's why I --
every day is so different here.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.762 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:18.198 line:92%
-So, that was intriguing to me.

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:19.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
I also kind of --
She -- She --

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:26.239
My mom, who I -- we all adored,
at the end of her life said,

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:26.773 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"I'm...

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:29.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like
I've accomplished nothing."

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:30.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-And I think that was

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:33.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
because she felt unfulfilled
as a person.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:37.250
I mean, she'd been a --
our mother and a wonderful wife.

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:41.788
And -- And I thought of her as I
was doing this -- this role --

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:44.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
someone who
is in the background,

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.058 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
holding the coat,

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:48.561 size:88% position:44%
helping with the glasses
and the pills until...

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:50.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's not good anymore.
-Right.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.932
This film takes place over
a very short period of time.

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:55.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-But there is also a flashback

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:56.302 line:92%
to when this couple first meets,

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:58.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you mention your mother,
but your daughter plays

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:02.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
the young version
of the character -- Annie.

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:04.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-That must have been exciting.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was.
-Yeah.

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:06.613 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-I was so proud of her.

00:04:06.613 --> 00:04:07.647 size:78% position:39% line:92%
She also, you know --

00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:12.185
I mean, it's really hard to be
the daughter of a famous person

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:14.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
and wanting to do
the same thing.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:19.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I -- I thought twice about
letting our director know

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:20.193 size:88% position:44% line:92%
that she was an actress,

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:22.729
'cause I knew that he was having
a hard time casting.

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:24.797
And I, you know, I kind of said,
"Well, you know, my...

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:26.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
[Whispering]
...my daughter's an actress."

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
And -- And that was it.

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:32.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then -- And then
she had three screen tests

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:34.407 line:92%
and a three-hour lunch with him,

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:35.475 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and she got the part.

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:38.745
And I was so proud of her.
She's -- She's beautiful.

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:39.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She's wonderful in it.
-Yeah.

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:41.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She really is.
You have reason to be proud.

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:44.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
Jonathan Pryce plays
your husband, as I mentioned.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:47.553
And you have never worked
together before, right?

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:48.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
And yet...
-No.

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:50.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...been in this business
for a -- a long time.

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:50.990 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Running a parallel career
with him, pretty much.

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:55.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. We --
We've been in the same time.

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:57.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you guys have
a love scene in the film,

00:04:57.497 --> 00:04:59.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that was
the first thing you shot?

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The first thing we shot.
-Wow.

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:03.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
What's that like?

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:06.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Um...well, it was fun.
-Yeah.

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:07.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Good.

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:10.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
That -- I feel like
that's a very good indicator

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:11.377 line:92%
of how the rest of the movie --

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:14.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Luckily for everyone,
we didn't have to get naked.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.949 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:18.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yes, that, would have been --
No, no.

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:22.155
But it -- it -- you know,
I think we both thought,

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:24.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Okay. We're pros.
We don't have to get all,

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:27.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
kind of nervous about it.

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:29.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Lord knows
we've done this before,

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:30.496 size:78% position:39% line:92%
so let's just do it."

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:31.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, well, that's good.
-Yeah.

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:35.101
-That seems to be a good advice
for anyone in a film.

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:38.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And we've done this before
in each of our lives.

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:40.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:43.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your -- Your daughter Annie
also got married.

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:44.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She did.
-And I heard you were --

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:47.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were reading a book
at the wedding.

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:49.082 size:88% position:44%
And when I first heard
you were reading a book,

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:50.850
I thought, "Oh, you know, Glenn,
you know, there's --"

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:53.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It wasn't at the wedding.
-It was the next day.

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:54.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was the next day...
-Okay.

00:05:54.287 --> 00:05:55.888
-...around the pool...
-But, still, I thought --

00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:58.024
-...with quite a bit of tequila.
-Okay.

00:05:58.024 --> 00:05:59.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
See, no one had told me that.

00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:01.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I thought,
"Oh, Glenn, you know,

00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:02.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
she's such an intellectual."
-Yes.

00:06:02.562 --> 00:06:03.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"She's probably reading
a book of poems.

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:06.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's something that's
going to inspire this couple."

00:06:06.099 --> 00:06:07.433
-There's a certain poetry, yeah.
-But we actually --

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:09.669 size:81% position:41%
you brought the book
that you were reading.

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:12.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now that I know --
it's a poolside tequila book.

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:14.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's Called
"Farts: A Spotter's Guide."

00:06:14.741 --> 00:06:17.043 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:20.012
Fred, do you think you could
maybe guess what this is about?

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:21.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It seems pretty serious.
-What?

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:24.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Very, very serious book.
-So, this is about --

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you were --
You were just playing this --

00:06:26.452 --> 00:06:29.288
Was -- Were people enjoyed to --
by your fart joke.

00:06:29.288 --> 00:06:30.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was hilarious.
-Yeah.

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:33.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Everyone was laughing a lot.
-Okay, that's good.

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:35.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
Thank you for sharing

00:06:35.728 --> 00:06:37.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
the part of Glenn Close...
-Yeah.

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:38.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...that we didn't know
was out there.

00:06:38.131 --> 00:06:39.665 size:75% position:38%
-Well, are you going
to do one of them?

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:40.433 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, I'll do one.

00:06:40.433 --> 00:06:41.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, by the way,
this is not --

00:06:41.768 --> 00:06:43.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They also have Latin names,
which I think's --

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:48.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay. So, here is the
"Flight of the Buttock Bees."

00:06:48.107 --> 00:06:52.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is
analretentivenus producili.

00:06:52.412 --> 00:06:54.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
Wait, hold on.
-Do it on the microphone.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:55.114 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:57.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Static crackling ]
No.

00:06:57.784 --> 00:07:00.887 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:01.421 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I think --

00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:04.157
Glenn, I think you wore out
the batteries at the wedding.

00:07:04.157 --> 00:07:05.958 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

